1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,356
At the end of a busy

2
00:00:01,381 --> 00:00:03,304
day, every store owner asks the

3
00:00:03,325 --> 00:00:04,149
same question.

4
00:00:04,444 --> 00:00:06,376
Where is my money right now?

5
00:00:06,653 --> 00:00:08,841
Cash and wallet answers that.

6
00:00:09,127 --> 00:00:11,204
It follows every peso, from the

7
00:00:11,226 --> 00:00:13,248
moment a customer pays, to the

8
00:00:13,270 --> 00:00:15,131
drawer, to the bank, and to

9
00:00:15,149 --> 00:00:15,832
the owner.

10
00:00:16,117 --> 00:00:18,210
It lives under five tabs.

11
00:00:18,498 --> 00:00:19,918
Today's drawer.

12
00:00:20,227 --> 00:00:21,725
Where money is.

13
00:00:22,007 --> 00:00:23,540
Cash in and out.

14
00:00:23,826 --> 00:00:25,552
Shifts and counts.

15
00:00:25,860 --> 00:00:27,536
And Cash on hand.

16
00:00:27,830 --> 00:00:30,021
Let's walk through them, one role

17
00:00:30,048 --> 00:00:30,793
at a time.

18
00:00:31,674 --> 00:00:34,016
First, three words you will hear

19
00:00:34,046 --> 00:00:34,564
a lot.

20
00:00:34,843 --> 00:00:36,627
The cash drawer is the physical

21
00:00:36,666 --> 00:00:37,738
cash in the store.

22
00:00:38,019 --> 00:00:39,865
Each cashier has their own tray,

23
00:00:39,892 --> 00:00:41,826
and together they make the store's

24
00:00:41,861 --> 00:00:42,258
drawer.

25
00:00:42,543 --> 00:00:44,813
Payment channels are where non cash

26
00:00:44,839 --> 00:00:47,142
payments land, like a card terminal,

27
00:00:47,190 --> 00:00:48,362
GCash, or a bank.

28
00:00:48,643 --> 00:00:50,124
And Cash on hand is the

29
00:00:50,144 --> 00:00:52,314
business's cash that the owner holds,

30
00:00:52,346 --> 00:00:53,715
outside of every store.

31
00:00:53,997 --> 00:00:55,522
One more idea.

32
00:00:55,821 --> 00:00:57,382
Expected is what the app says

33
00:00:57,403 --> 00:00:58,690
should be in the drawer.

34
00:00:58,972 --> 00:01:01,344
Counted is what you actually count.

35
00:01:01,631 --> 00:01:03,854
If counted is less, you are

36
00:01:03,881 --> 00:01:04,368
short.

37
00:01:04,660 --> 00:01:06,514
If it is more, you are

38
00:01:06,540 --> 00:01:06,958
over.

39
00:01:07,844 --> 00:01:09,800
Four roles use this, and each

40
00:01:09,826 --> 00:01:11,557
one sees a different part.

41
00:01:11,838 --> 00:01:14,093
A cashier handles only their own

42
00:01:14,117 --> 00:01:14,547
shift.

43
00:01:14,834 --> 00:01:17,092
A supervisor watches the whole store

44
00:01:17,122 --> 00:01:19,584
drawer, and checks the cashiers' counts.

45
00:01:19,872 --> 00:01:21,659
A manager does that too, and

46
00:01:21,680 --> 00:01:23,571
also ends the store's day, and

47
00:01:23,592 --> 00:01:25,168
records money in and out.

48
00:01:25,443 --> 00:01:27,383
The owner, or an admin, sees

49
00:01:27,410 --> 00:01:29,570
every store, holds Cash on hand,

50
00:01:29,602 --> 00:01:31,265
and is the only one who

51
00:01:31,288 --> 00:01:33,046
moves money between stores.

52
00:01:33,936 --> 00:01:35,805
Here is a cashier's day.

53
00:01:36,085 --> 00:01:38,460
Open Today's drawer, and under My

54
00:01:38,479 --> 00:01:40,536
shift, choose Start my shift.

55
00:01:40,824 --> 00:01:43,387
Enter your opening cash, here five

56
00:01:43,418 --> 00:01:44,453
hundred pesos.

57
00:01:44,743 --> 00:01:46,616
You can also start from the

58
00:01:46,639 --> 00:01:47,388
Sales page.

59
00:01:47,669 --> 00:01:49,467
Now sell as usual.

60
00:01:49,768 --> 00:01:51,660
Every cash sale adds to your

61
00:01:51,686 --> 00:01:52,679
tray's Expected.

62
00:01:52,977 --> 00:01:54,858
When you are done, choose End

63
00:01:54,879 --> 00:01:56,703
my shift, and count the cash

64
00:01:56,728 --> 00:01:57,596
in your tray.

65
00:01:57,876 --> 00:01:59,525
You don't need a PIN.

66
00:01:59,805 --> 00:02:02,079
If your count matches, you are

67
00:02:02,104 --> 00:02:02,504
done.

68
00:02:02,789 --> 00:02:04,327
If it is short or over,

69
00:02:04,356 --> 00:02:06,425
the shift shows Needs review, and

70
00:02:06,445 --> 00:02:07,887
a supervisor checks it.

71
00:02:08,158 --> 00:02:10,188
You can keep working meanwhile.

72
00:02:11,092 --> 00:02:13,512
Every shift follows the same path.

73
00:02:13,796 --> 00:02:15,333
It starts Open.

74
00:02:15,630 --> 00:02:18,197
When the cashier counts, it becomes

75
00:02:18,242 --> 00:02:18,699
Ended.

76
00:02:18,989 --> 00:02:20,647
If the count is off, it

77
00:02:20,665 --> 00:02:22,078
goes to Needs review.

78
00:02:22,368 --> 00:02:24,523
A supervisor then approves it, or

79
00:02:24,541 --> 00:02:26,399
sends it back for a recount.

80
00:02:26,692 --> 00:02:28,305
When it is sent back, the

81
00:02:28,326 --> 00:02:30,442
cashier counts again, and the shift

82
00:02:30,470 --> 00:02:32,173
goes through the same steps.

83
00:02:32,456 --> 00:02:34,168
If a cashier forgets to end

84
00:02:34,188 --> 00:02:36,385
their shift, it shows under Forgotten

85
00:02:36,430 --> 00:02:38,248
shifts, so someone can end it

86
00:02:38,265 --> 00:02:38,847
for them.

87
00:02:39,126 --> 00:02:40,584
And if a shift was ended

88
00:02:40,611 --> 00:02:42,503
on another device, the Sales page

89
00:02:42,526 --> 00:02:44,423
tells you, instead of letting you

90
00:02:44,442 --> 00:02:45,800
sell on a closed shift.

91
00:02:46,681 --> 00:02:48,951
A supervisor opens Today's drawer and

92
00:02:48,972 --> 00:02:50,292
sees the whole store.

93
00:02:50,575 --> 00:02:52,557
Cash in drawers is every tray

94
00:02:52,584 --> 00:02:53,232
added up.

95
00:02:53,504 --> 00:02:55,364
Cash sales today is what went

96
00:02:55,389 --> 00:02:56,446
into the drawers.

97
00:02:56,738 --> 00:02:58,763
Card, e-wallet and bank is money

98
00:02:58,793 --> 00:03:00,964
that went past the drawer, straight

99
00:03:01,006 --> 00:03:01,965
into a channel.

100
00:03:02,257 --> 00:03:04,227
Counts off shows how many counts

101
00:03:04,260 --> 00:03:05,148
need a review.

102
00:03:05,435 --> 00:03:07,558
A supervisor can set the opening

103
00:03:07,598 --> 00:03:09,342
cash, and do a spot check

104
00:03:09,373 --> 00:03:10,008
any time.

105
00:03:10,289 --> 00:03:12,038
A spot check counts the drawer

106
00:03:12,068 --> 00:03:13,373
without ending anything.

107
00:03:13,665 --> 00:03:15,982
Then, on Shifts and counts, open

108
00:03:16,010 --> 00:03:17,892
a count that needs review.

109
00:03:18,185 --> 00:03:20,429
Look at Expected, Counted, and the

110
00:03:20,451 --> 00:03:21,112
Difference.

111
00:03:21,419 --> 00:03:23,148
Approve it with a note, or

112
00:03:23,165 --> 00:03:24,921
send it back for a recount.

113
00:03:25,213 --> 00:03:27,532
A supervisor only sees their own

114
00:03:27,556 --> 00:03:27,943
team.

115
00:03:28,828 --> 00:03:30,841
When every cashier has ended their

116
00:03:30,869 --> 00:03:32,924
shift, the manager ends the store's

117
00:03:32,959 --> 00:03:33,234
day.

118
00:03:33,508 --> 00:03:35,538
Choose End the store's day, and

119
00:03:35,559 --> 00:03:36,982
enter the final count.

120
00:03:37,267 --> 00:03:39,509
Then decide where the cash goes.

121
00:03:39,792 --> 00:03:41,561
Cash out sends it to Cash

122
00:03:41,588 --> 00:03:43,180
on hand, for the owner.

123
00:03:43,466 --> 00:03:45,673
The drawer starts tomorrow empty.

124
00:03:45,960 --> 00:03:47,730
Keep as opening leaves it in

125
00:03:47,746 --> 00:03:50,064
the drawer, as tomorrow's opening cash.

126
00:03:50,343 --> 00:03:52,336
Once the day is closed, nothing

127
00:03:52,375 --> 00:03:54,011
more can be added to it.

128
00:03:54,282 --> 00:03:55,869
If you made a mistake, a

129
00:03:55,882 --> 00:03:57,822
manager or admin can reopen the

130
00:03:57,843 --> 00:03:59,044
day, with a reason.

131
00:03:59,931 --> 00:04:02,334
Not all money comes from sales.

132
00:04:02,625 --> 00:04:04,245
On Cash in and out, a

133
00:04:04,259 --> 00:04:05,976
manager records the rest.

134
00:04:06,259 --> 00:04:08,584
Cash in, for example Added float,

135
00:04:08,621 --> 00:04:10,492
when you put in change or

136
00:04:10,511 --> 00:04:11,359
small bills.

137
00:04:11,647 --> 00:04:14,276
Cash out, for example Owner took

138
00:04:14,309 --> 00:04:14,749
cash.

139
00:04:15,037 --> 00:04:16,916
Move, to send money between the

140
00:04:16,936 --> 00:04:19,042
drawer and the store's own channels,

141
00:04:19,086 --> 00:04:21,157
like depositing cash into the bank.

142
00:04:21,435 --> 00:04:23,386
Before you save, the app shows

143
00:04:23,416 --> 00:04:25,487
the balance before and after, so

144
00:04:25,504 --> 00:04:27,335
you see exactly what changes.

145
00:04:27,628 --> 00:04:29,868
Other pages add lines here too.

146
00:04:30,147 --> 00:04:32,293
An expense, a supplier payment, or

147
00:04:32,310 --> 00:04:34,083
a loan payment all show up,

148
00:04:34,104 --> 00:04:36,189
because they also took money from

149
00:04:36,214 --> 00:04:36,915
the drawer.

150
00:04:37,803 --> 00:04:39,554
Where money is puts it all

151
00:04:39,575 --> 00:04:40,503
on one screen.

152
00:04:40,792 --> 00:04:42,587
For each store, you see the

153
00:04:42,608 --> 00:04:44,981
cash drawer, every e-wallet, and every

154
00:04:45,011 --> 00:04:47,122
bank and card terminal, each with

155
00:04:47,148 --> 00:04:48,863
its balance and a subtotal.

156
00:04:49,160 --> 00:04:51,398
The owner sees every store side

157
00:04:51,426 --> 00:04:53,421
by side, plus Cash on hand.

158
00:04:53,704 --> 00:04:55,217
This is the answer to the

159
00:04:55,236 --> 00:04:56,646
question we started with.

160
00:04:56,923 --> 00:04:58,855
Where is my money right now?

161
00:04:59,732 --> 00:05:01,487
Now the owner's part.

162
00:05:01,776 --> 00:05:04,017
Money only moves between stores that

163
00:05:04,042 --> 00:05:04,654
allow it.

164
00:05:04,925 --> 00:05:07,751
Go to Inventory, then Locations.

165
00:05:08,074 --> 00:05:10,115
Edit each store, and turn on

166
00:05:10,134 --> 00:05:11,450
Can transfer money.

167
00:05:11,738 --> 00:05:13,675
Do this for both stores.

168
00:05:13,973 --> 00:05:15,406
One more rule.

169
00:05:15,702 --> 00:05:17,212
You can't move money into or

170
00:05:17,226 --> 00:05:18,427
out of a day that has

171
00:05:18,445 --> 00:05:19,418
already been ended.

172
00:05:20,296 --> 00:05:21,937
There are three ways to move

173
00:05:21,959 --> 00:05:23,260
money to another store.

174
00:05:23,540 --> 00:05:25,495
Only one of them passes through

175
00:05:25,533 --> 00:05:26,395
Cash on hand.

176
00:05:26,674 --> 00:05:27,695
One.

177
00:05:28,034 --> 00:05:30,746
Transfer, on Cash in and out.

178
00:05:31,033 --> 00:05:32,681
Pick the other store and the

179
00:05:32,700 --> 00:05:34,586
place, drawer or channel, and the

180
00:05:34,605 --> 00:05:36,051
money goes straight there.

181
00:05:36,331 --> 00:05:37,246
Two.

182
00:05:37,576 --> 00:05:39,633
Owner took cash, and choose Into

183
00:05:39,658 --> 00:05:41,222
the other store's drawer.

184
00:05:41,510 --> 00:05:43,702
The owner carries the cash over.

185
00:05:43,984 --> 00:05:45,882
This only works from the cash

186
00:05:45,907 --> 00:05:46,350
drawer.

187
00:05:46,638 --> 00:05:47,649
Three.

188
00:05:47,987 --> 00:05:49,724
Through Cash on hand.

189
00:05:50,012 --> 00:05:51,686
The cash comes in first, and

190
00:05:51,706 --> 00:05:53,529
later the owner chooses Move to

191
00:05:53,545 --> 00:05:55,256
a store, and picks its drawer

192
00:05:55,287 --> 00:05:56,647
or one of its channels.

193
00:05:57,540 --> 00:05:59,451
Cash on hand is the owner's

194
00:05:59,492 --> 00:05:59,862
safe.

195
00:06:00,144 --> 00:06:02,104
Money gets in two ways.

196
00:06:02,393 --> 00:06:04,104
When a manager chooses Cash out

197
00:06:04,122 --> 00:06:05,420
at the end of the day.

198
00:06:05,692 --> 00:06:07,409
Or when the owner collects an

199
00:06:07,424 --> 00:06:09,648
approved shift, from Waiting to collect.

200
00:06:09,936 --> 00:06:12,028
Money goes out three ways.

201
00:06:12,315 --> 00:06:13,791
Move to a store sends it

202
00:06:13,807 --> 00:06:15,453
back to a drawer or channel.

203
00:06:15,741 --> 00:06:17,778
Correction fixes a mistake.

204
00:06:18,080 --> 00:06:19,659
And Owner used it means the

205
00:06:19,678 --> 00:06:21,658
owner spent it outside the business.

206
00:06:21,949 --> 00:06:23,345
Remember this.

207
00:06:23,643 --> 00:06:25,900
Collecting cash, and moving it back

208
00:06:25,927 --> 00:06:27,740
to a store, does not change

209
00:06:27,775 --> 00:06:28,447
the books.

210
00:06:28,732 --> 00:06:30,812
It is still the business's money.

211
00:06:31,096 --> 00:06:32,897
Only Owner used it takes money

212
00:06:32,925 --> 00:06:34,117
out of the business.

213
00:06:35,010 --> 00:06:37,287
Finally, the big picture.

214
00:06:37,599 --> 00:06:39,744
Under Finance, Money in and out

215
00:06:39,767 --> 00:06:41,218
shows your cash flow.

216
00:06:41,500 --> 00:06:43,697
Money in is sales, credit payments,

217
00:06:43,744 --> 00:06:45,700
loans, and money the owner put

218
00:06:45,722 --> 00:06:45,968
in.

219
00:06:46,239 --> 00:06:48,827
Money out is expenses, suppliers, loan

220
00:06:48,855 --> 00:06:51,317
payments, equipment, and owner draws.

221
00:06:51,604 --> 00:06:53,626
Moving money between your own drawers,

222
00:06:53,663 --> 00:06:55,295
channels, and Cash on hand is

223
00:06:55,309 --> 00:06:56,896
not on this list, because it

224
00:06:56,910 --> 00:06:58,197
never left the business.

225
00:06:58,487 --> 00:07:00,075
And there is a section called

226
00:07:00,104 --> 00:07:01,948
Why profit and money are different.

227
00:07:02,241 --> 00:07:03,897
You can make a profit, and

228
00:07:03,918 --> 00:07:05,578
still be short on cash, if

229
00:07:05,594 --> 00:07:07,039
it is tied up in stock

230
00:07:07,067 --> 00:07:08,402
or in customer credit.

231
00:07:09,290 --> 00:07:11,645
So, which way to move money?

232
00:07:11,939 --> 00:07:13,878
If the other store needs it

233
00:07:13,896 --> 00:07:15,112
now, use Transfer.

234
00:07:15,413 --> 00:07:17,217
If you are carrying cash from

235
00:07:17,241 --> 00:07:19,193
one drawer to another, use Owner

236
00:07:19,222 --> 00:07:19,854
took cash.

237
00:07:20,132 --> 00:07:22,246
If you collect first and decide

238
00:07:22,282 --> 00:07:23,948
later, use Cash on hand.

239
00:07:24,230 --> 00:07:25,475
To recap.

240
00:07:25,795 --> 00:07:28,416
Cashiers start, sell, and count their

241
00:07:28,450 --> 00:07:29,140
own tray.

242
00:07:29,424 --> 00:07:31,776
Supervisors check the drawer and the

243
00:07:31,798 --> 00:07:32,255
counts.

244
00:07:32,545 --> 00:07:34,427
Managers end the store's day and

245
00:07:34,446 --> 00:07:35,886
record money in and out.

246
00:07:36,159 --> 00:07:38,209
And the owner sees every store,

247
00:07:38,244 --> 00:07:40,189
keeps Cash on hand, and moves

248
00:07:40,220 --> 00:07:41,552
money between stores.

249
00:07:41,842 --> 00:07:43,674
That's Cash and wallet.
